# .cursorrules — Cursor & Windsurf AI Rules for AJWMES

You are pair programming on the AJW Marine Electrical Services codebase. Follow these rules strictly:

## 1. Tech Stack & Environment
- Runtime: Node >=24.12.0
- Framework: React 19, TypeScript strict mode (^7.0.2), Vite 8, Tailwind CSS v4 (@tailwindcss/vite).
- Cloud: Firebase v13 (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Hosting), Firebase Cloud Functions 2nd Gen (`functions/` in `europe-west2` with `firebase-admin ^14.5.0` & `firebase-functions ^7.4.0`), Google GenAI SDK (@google/genai).
- Do NOT generate legacy config files like `tailwind.config.js` or `postcss.config.js`.

## 2. Code Structure & Conventions
- Pure business logic belongs in `src/utils/` as standalone, side-effect-free pure functions.
- Domain types are strictly centralized in `src/types/index.ts` (re-exported in `src/types.ts`).
- Route guards and action authorization must use `src/lib/rbac.ts` (`canAccessRoute`, `canPerformAction`) across all 6 roles (`guest`, `client`, `technician`, `postal`, `admin`, `site`) and `functions/src/authMiddleware.ts` on the server.
- LocalStorage keys must always be scoped using `src/lib/envStorage.ts` (`getScopedStorageKey`). Never use raw strings in `localStorage`.

## 3. Offline Resilience & Server Gateways
- Technicians work offline on pontoon berths and inside steel boats.
- Mutations must pass through `src/lib/offlineSync.ts`.
- Firestore connection failures (e.g. Code 14 UNAVAILABLE) and Cloud Function disconnects (`sendEmail`, `getShippingRates`, `generateShippingLabel`) must never crash the UI or throw unhandled promise rejections — always degrade gracefully to local caches / simulated fallbacks.
- True secrets (`RESEND_API_KEY`, `SHIPSTATION_API_KEY`, `SHIPSTATION_API_SECRET`, Stripe `sk_...`) must never be exposed in `VITE_*` client variables; they reside in Google Secret Manager (`functions/src/index.ts`).

## 4. Testing & Verification Checklist
- Any modification to business logic requires companion unit tests in `src/utils/<name>.test.ts` (and `src/lib/<name>.test.ts` or `functions/src/<name>.test.ts` for service/cloud layers).
- Unit tests use Node's built-in test runner via `npm run test:unit` (309 tests across 25 suites) and `npm run test:functions` (21 tests across 2 suites — 330 total unit tests).
- All new interactive UI controls must have `data-testid` attributes for Playwright E2E tests (21 spec files in `tests/` + 1 training video spec in `tests/training/` across 16 Page Object Models in `tests/pages/`).
- Always run `npm run lint`, `npm run test:unit`, `npm run test:functions`, and `npm run validate` to verify changes before presenting your solution.
